     "result_text_tail": "*The $9.5M cash figure:** the pack doesn't say whether it already includes today's $0.4M a month burn, so the cash slide shows both readings. Both breach the 12-month runway floor.\n- **Strongest alternative:** I tested a one-store pilot and Zipcart's pricing moves, and rejected both on the slides. I couldn't put a number on the proposed minimum pay rules for riders. They would only make every loss bigger, so the loss figures in the deck understate the problem.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **The software path also has a deadline.** Even with the software-only plan, cash reaches the 12-month floor in about 14 months unless new contracts bring the burn down. That's why one next step is a burn plan.\n- **I rendered with a patched copy of the skill's renderer** (`work/skill_scripts/`), because the plugin folder is read-only. The only change shows per-order dollar amounts to the cent, so the cards match the text and the equations add up on screen.\n- **One QA warning is left, and it's expected.** The pack writes \"two of the three cities\" in words, so the checker can't match the number 2 against it.\n- **I couldn't open the slides to look at them**, because PowerPoint isn't available here. The renderer reports no layout problems, but please flip through the deck once in PowerPoint.\n- **The editable spec is `work/parcelbird-now.json`**, generated by `work/build_spec.py`.\n\nI can switch the theme, add a backup slide comparing the low, base and high cases, or tighten any slide you want to change."
    }
